WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.916
Welcome to the Beginner's Guide
for Armored Core six.

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:05.083
By the end of this video,

00:00:05.083 --> 00:00:09.083
you'll understand what it means
to play Armored Core at a higher level.

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:10.783
You'll be faster at the controls.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:14.233
You'll know how
to put together a powerful AC,

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:18.649
and you'll be able to quickly read
and adapt to any situation.

00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:21.583
Feel free to skip ahead to a section
that you're more interested in.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:25.383
But for now,
let's get started at the beginning.

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:29.116
First, let's get to grips
with the controls.

00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:30.433
This guide will assume that you're

00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:34.599
using the default type A
control assignment, with a controller,

00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:38.766
but mouse and keyboard can be
an effective means of control as well.

00:00:38.766 --> 00:00:41.499
If you're playing on PC,
be sure to open up the settings menu

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:45.283
and scroll down to input device settings
where you can ensure that

00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:49.083
your button prompts are being properly
displayed for the input you're using.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:50.649
And while you're here in the settings,

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:54.699
I also like to go into the camera
settings and turn camera speed to ten.

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:56.616
That's because turning quickly to face

00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:59.233
enemies is very important
in Armored Core,

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:00.849
 as you'll soon learn.

00:01:00.849 --> 00:01:05.149
So you've just crash landed on Rubicon
and your AC has taken damage.

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:08.899
It's AP, which stands for Armor
Points, can be viewed here

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:10.866
to instantly repair your AC.

00:01:10.866 --> 00:01:12.883
Press up on the d-pad.

00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.733
This consumes a repair charge, seen here

00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:19.633
which instantly heals
your AC for a flat 4000 AP.

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:23.449
The bar underneath shows the delay
before you can repair your AC again.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.366
And it's important to note

00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:27.466
that you can't repair your AC
while firing your weaponry.

00:01:27.466 --> 00:01:29.716
Be sure to keep your AC
topped up on health,

00:01:29.716 --> 00:01:32.566
especially if you think an enemy
is capable of

00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:36.099
extremely damaging attacks,
which many of them are.

00:01:36.099 --> 00:01:37.866
If you think enemies might be nearby,

00:01:37.866 --> 00:01:41.666
you can press down on the d-pad
to scan your environment.

00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:44.999
Again, The bar below shows how often you can
use this, 

00:01:44.999 --> 00:01:46.499
so there’s no enemies nearby.

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:51.849
But if there was, you could fire at them
with any of one of your four weapon slots.

00:01:51.849 --> 00:01:55.249
Right now we're equipped
with an assault rifle in our right hand,

00:01:55.249 --> 00:02:00.149
a missile launcher on our right shoulder,
and a laser blade on our left arm.

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:04.449
Your back triggers activate your left and
right arm weapons, and your front bumpers

00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:07.149
activate your left and right back weapons.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:10.966
Note how your total ammunition
depletes in the bottom right of the screen

00:02:10.966 --> 00:02:16.866
and how your current magazine capacity
is affected here around your lock-on.

00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:18.499
Let's get moving.

00:02:18.499 --> 00:02:20.982
So when at a standstill, your glide
boosters are disengaged and you can walk.

00:02:20.982 --> 00:02:23.599
So when at a standstill, your glide
boosters are disengaged and you can walk.

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:28.816
However, you'll often want to press circle
or B to manually engage your boosters

00:02:28.816 --> 00:02:33.949
while grounded, as that is a superior
form of movement, especially in combat.

00:02:33.949 --> 00:02:36.582
Note that these glide boosters
automatically toggle

00:02:36.582 --> 00:02:38.599
on when you quick boost as well.

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:42.882
The indicator for glide boosting is seen
here. We’ll need to ascend

00:02:42.882 --> 00:02:46.066
to reach our objective marker,
which is shown here.

00:02:46.066 --> 00:02:50.682
Pressing X or A while grounded
will cause you to jump with your leg part

00:02:50.682 --> 00:02:53.415
and after that jump holding X or A

00:02:53.415 --> 00:02:56.415
will cause you to ascend
with your boosters.

00:02:56.415 --> 00:03:00.582
Ascending requires energy
which is being depleted here.

00:03:00.582 --> 00:03:03.165
Energy consumption 
is paused while descending,

00:03:03.165 --> 00:03:06.965
and your energy recovers really rapidly
while you're grounded.

00:03:06.965 --> 00:03:09.915
If you fully deplete your energy bar,
it will go red

00:03:09.915 --> 00:03:12.882
and energy will not recover
for a short duration.

00:03:12.882 --> 00:03:16.249
So you should generally try
to avoid fully depleting

00:03:16.249 --> 00:03:19.265
your energy bar
if possible, in the heat of combat.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.849
Keep an ear out for warning
sounds as well.

00:03:21.849 --> 00:03:24.582
The warning for loss of energy is

00:03:24.582 --> 00:03:29.115
just one sound
that can give you crucial information.

00:03:29.115 --> 00:03:30.965
Now let's fight some enemies 

00:03:30.965 --> 00:03:33.882
In this game,
Lock on is automatic when you're in range.

00:03:33.882 --> 00:03:35.382
And the enemy closest

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:39.615
to the center of your screen
will be locked onto by moving the camera.

00:03:39.615 --> 00:03:41.465
You can target other enemies

00:03:41.465 --> 00:03:45.215
by aligning them more closely
with the center of your screen.

00:03:45.215 --> 00:03:48.282
This method of targeting
is particularly useful when taking out

00:03:48.282 --> 00:03:53.265
multiple enemies, as you might want some
to have priority over others.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:58.482
Our assault rifle is on our right arm,
so we fire it with R2 and take them out.

00:03:58.482 --> 00:04:03.349
However, in many cases you might prefer
a more automatic hard lock,

00:04:03.349 --> 00:04:07.749
and for this you can enable target assist
by pressing R3

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:11.498
In this mode,
four crescents appear here and now.

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:15.282
When an enemy is in your sights,
you'll be hard locked onto them.

00:04:15.282 --> 00:04:19.398
In this state, your tracking accuracy
is slightly reduced,

00:04:19.398 --> 00:04:21.498
so your shots might not hit your target

00:04:21.498 --> 00:04:25.515
as effectively
as if you didn't have target Assist on.

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:28.548
However, this way
your enemy is kept in your sights

00:04:28.548 --> 00:04:31.998
at all times and you don't need
to touch the thumbstick at all.

00:04:31.998 --> 00:04:33.048
Really.

00:04:33.048 --> 00:04:37.965
This is particularly useful when you're
fighting against a single difficult enemy,

00:04:37.965 --> 00:04:40.815
especially if that enemy
has dangerous attacks

00:04:40.815 --> 00:04:45.315
that require you to focus on
dodging and flight instead.

00:04:45.315 --> 00:04:49.365
One thing to note in the center
of our lock on is this yellow crescent.

00:04:49.365 --> 00:04:50.982
That's your missile marker.

00:04:50.982 --> 00:04:53.715
And the number represents
how many missiles

00:04:53.715 --> 00:04:57.048
are chambered
and ready to be fired at this enemy.

00:04:57.048 --> 00:05:02.198
Only try and fire your missiles once
the yellow bar has fully loaded like this.

00:05:02.198 --> 00:05:04.598
When the number appears,
you're fully locked on.

00:05:04.598 --> 00:05:10.065
And while you can fire the missiles before
this, they won't track very well at all.

00:05:10.065 --> 00:05:12.765
Our missiles are attached
to our right back.

00:05:12.765 --> 00:05:18.165
So the marker appears in the top right,
and we can press R1 to fire them.

00:05:18.165 --> 00:05:19.815
But if you're against multiple enemies,

00:05:19.815 --> 00:05:23.615
you might not want to fire
all your missiles at just one enemy.

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:28.148
Instead, what you can do
is hold down the fire button like this.

00:05:28.148 --> 00:05:31.098
This will acquire a multi lock and split

00:05:31.098 --> 00:05:35.131
your missiles evenly to all enemies
within your field of view.

00:05:35.131 --> 00:05:38.898
Lastly, our starter build is equipped
with a laser blade on its left hand.

00:05:38.898 --> 00:05:42.281
This means we can tap L2 to swing it
and it will boost us

00:05:42.281 --> 00:05:46.148
towards any locked enemy
as far as our energy will allow.

00:05:46.148 --> 00:05:50.348
All melee weapons can have their input
held for a charge attack and

00:05:50.348 --> 00:05:55.215
this one in particular can be swung twice
if L2 is pressed in succession.

00:05:55.215 --> 00:05:58.815
After attacks,
the blade also overheats, meaning

00:05:58.815 --> 00:06:02.148
it can't be used for a short
period of time.

00:06:02.148 --> 00:06:04.415
For every encounter,
you should be finding a way

00:06:04.415 --> 00:06:08.215
to maximize efficient use of every weapon
you have equipped. 

00:06:08.215 --> 00:06:11.465
With this build,
we use multi lock missiles to initiate.

00:06:11.465 --> 00:06:14.598
We fire the assault rifle
when we're in range

00:06:14.598 --> 00:06:16.748
and we use the blade whenever we spy

00:06:16.748 --> 00:06:18.765
a safe opening.

00:06:22.631 --> 00:06:24.198
So we've just finished a fight

00:06:24.198 --> 00:06:26.531
and our assault rifle is low on ammo.

00:06:26.531 --> 00:06:30.798
Many weapons only reload automatically
when their magazines are empty.

00:06:30.798 --> 00:06:33.998
So you should make a habit of manually
reloading

00:06:33.998 --> 00:06:37.215
to ensure that you are topped up
between fights.

00:06:37.215 --> 00:06:40.965
Manual reloads can be done by holding down
triangle or Y

00:06:40.965 --> 00:06:45.348
and tapping the fire button for the weapon
that you want to reload.

00:06:45.348 --> 00:06:47.265
Let's head down to the city.

00:06:47.265 --> 00:06:49.365
This is called an assault boost.

00:06:49.365 --> 00:06:52.598
You perform this by pressing L3
and it propels

00:06:52.598 --> 00:06:54.665
you towards wherever you're aiming.

00:06:54.665 --> 00:06:56.115
Pull back on the left stick

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:59.264
 to cancel the assault boost,
like this.

00:06:59.264 --> 00:07:02.148
or tap the ascend button X or A

00:07:02.148 --> 00:07:05.714
to cancel your boost
while maintaining your forward momentum.

00:07:05.714 --> 00:07:06.998
Like this.

00:07:06.998 --> 00:07:10.398
Assault boosts are by far
the most efficient way to move around

00:07:10.398 --> 00:07:11.381
the map.

00:07:11.381 --> 00:07:15.614
However, where this ability really
excels is in combat.

00:07:15.614 --> 00:07:22.548
Assault boost is just an excellent tool
for closing the gap towards enemies.

00:07:22.548 --> 00:07:23.298
And if you have

00:07:23.298 --> 00:07:27.131
the energy to spare,
you can even dodge left or right during it

00:07:27.131 --> 00:07:31.398
by tapping the left
analog stick like this.

00:07:31.398 --> 00:07:32.748
But what makes assault boost

00:07:32.748 --> 00:07:36.614
truly powerful is that you can attack
as you assault boost

00:07:36.614 --> 00:07:41.298
and many attacks done during this time
deal increased impact damage

00:07:41.314 --> 00:07:45.281
meaning they'll be more effective
at breaking enemy guards.

00:07:45.281 --> 00:07:49.481
What's more, impact you receive during
this time is also lessened

00:07:49.481 --> 00:07:54.698
meaning you can assault boost
into many enemies with reckless abandon.

00:07:54.698 --> 00:07:58.848
So let's show this off against the next
two enemies who have shields.

00:07:58.848 --> 00:08:01.898
By combining our assault boost
with a blade attack,

00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:04.398
we can absolutely obliterate them.

00:08:04.398 --> 00:08:07.031
But let's keep the second one
alive for now.

00:08:07.031 --> 00:08:09.348
See the two meters above the enemy?

00:08:09.348 --> 00:08:12.714
This one shows the enemy's health,
and the second one shows 

00:08:12.714 --> 00:08:14.898
the enemy’s ACS Strain.

00:08:14.898 --> 00:08:18.764
ACS strain builds up orange like this
whenever you attack.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:22.864
And when the bar fills fully,
the enemy's guard is broken.

00:08:22.864 --> 00:08:27.797
In this state of ACS
overload, enemies take direct damage,

00:08:27.797 --> 00:08:31.181
which means any attack
you unleash in this moment

00:08:31.181 --> 00:08:34.097
is far more damaging to the enemy's
health.

00:08:34.097 --> 00:08:37.631
Naturally, enemies can do impact damage
to you as well,

00:08:37.631 --> 00:08:42.347
and your ACS strain will build up here
above your energy bar.

00:08:42.347 --> 00:08:46.931
If an enemy attack breaks your guard,
your AC will pause like this

00:08:46.931 --> 00:08:49.597
and you'll take additional damage as well

00:08:49.597 --> 00:08:51.581
to ensure that this doesn't happen

00:08:51.581 --> 00:08:56.797
You should try and maneuver for extended
periods where you don't take any damage.

00:08:56.797 --> 00:08:59.181
After a few seconds of no damage, 

00:08:59.181 --> 00:09:01.281
ACS strain will diminish 

00:09:01.281 --> 00:09:03.797
 and this is where
the environment often comes in handy.

00:09:03.797 --> 00:09:06.914
It's something you can use
to block attacks, giving you

00:09:06.914 --> 00:09:11.714
time to reduce ACS strain
and often to reload as well.

00:09:11.714 --> 00:09:14.981
But notice how my assault rifle
isn't doing much impact damage

00:09:14.981 --> 00:09:16.781
to this shielded enemy.

00:09:16.781 --> 00:09:20.714
That's because some weapons are better
at building up impacts than others.

00:09:20.714 --> 00:09:23.797
If I use my explosive missiles
or my blade,

00:09:23.797 --> 00:09:28.364
for example, then I can easily break
the guard of the target.

00:09:28.364 --> 00:09:29.047
The first

00:09:29.047 --> 00:09:31.447
true test of your skills
will be this 

00:09:31.447 --> 00:09:34.814
 the AH12-HC helicopter.

00:09:34.814 --> 00:09:37.031
In this fight, you'll have to use
everything you've learned.

00:09:37.031 --> 00:09:38.947
Plus another skill as well.

00:09:38.947 --> 00:09:42.464
The quick boost by tapping square or X,

00:09:42.464 --> 00:09:45.830
you'll be able to dash
for additional avoidance.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.664
It's worth noting that an Armored Core
there are no invincibility frames,

00:09:49.664 --> 00:09:50.947
however, So

00:09:50.947 --> 00:09:55.547
think of Quick Boost as a way to quickly
get distance away from an enemy's attack

00:09:55.547 --> 00:10:00.097
rather than an ability
that you use to dodge an enemy's attack.

00:10:00.097 --> 00:10:04.297
Quick boost is particularly useful,
while target assist is enabled

00:10:04.297 --> 00:10:08.497
because your thumb is free to tap
the boost button and I highly recommend

00:10:08.497 --> 00:10:11.897
putting target assist
on while you're fighting most boss battles

00:10:11.897 --> 00:10:14.647
because it's here
that you're going to have to pay special

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:18.347
attention to enemy movements and attacks.

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:22.630
So to recap in this fight, I'm
going to try and accomplish a few things.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:26.414
I'm going to use target assist to hard
lock onto the enemy,

00:10:26.414 --> 00:10:30.080
and I'm going to constantly fire
my assault rifle and missiles

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.414
pretty much as soon as they're available.

00:10:32.414 --> 00:10:36.730
I'm also going to do my best to assault
boost in and use my blade on cooldown.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.797
This is my main damage dealer in this fight.

00:10:39.797 --> 00:10:42.730
And when I return to the ground
to recover energy,

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:45.697
I'm going to do my best
to stay close to the enemy.

00:10:45.697 --> 00:10:49.847
I'm safe when I'm close and I'm safe
when I'm underneath the enemy.

00:10:49.847 --> 00:10:53.264
But if the enemy has distance on me,
I'm going to use the environment

00:10:53.264 --> 00:10:54.397
to my advantage.

00:10:54.397 --> 00:10:57.847
This is particularly useful
when you see warning signs like this,

00:10:57.847 --> 00:11:02.864
or if you just need a moment to reload
or repair or reposition.

00:11:02.864 --> 00:11:07.213
Coming up with a battle plan for bosses
can really work wonders in this game.

00:11:07.213 --> 00:11:11.147
So with this,
I should just naturally come out on top.

00:11:11.147 --> 00:11:12.847
Let's put this plan to the test.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.897
After the mission is complete,
you'll obtain your reward.

00:12:04.897 --> 00:12:09.380
COAM credits,
minus the ammunition and repair costs

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:13.363
that were incurred
during your successful mission attempt.

00:12:13.363 --> 00:12:15.730
After each mission, you'll return to this.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:16.747
The garage.

00:12:16.747 --> 00:12:21.880
Here, players can have some downtime and
prepare for success in future missions.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.547
Right now we've just finished Mission one
and the part shop

00:12:25.547 --> 00:12:30.246
isn't open to us, so let's
check out the Sortie menu instead.

00:12:30.246 --> 00:12:33.696
Here you can and should do a few things.

00:12:33.696 --> 00:12:36.096
First, head to the training simulator.

00:12:36.096 --> 00:12:40.363
Here you can defeat some basic enemies
and learn some invaluable lessons

00:12:40.363 --> 00:12:41.380
about the game.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:45.013
If you ever need to review these lessons,
then you can always display

00:12:45.013 --> 00:12:48.846
the license menu in the garage
by pressing triangle or Y.

00:12:48.846 --> 00:12:51.463
Then navigate down to the tip screen.

00:12:51.463 --> 00:12:56.263
By completing training, you'll often be
rewarded with powerful new parts for your AC.

00:12:56.263 --> 00:12:59.713
So I highly recommend
completing new training missions

00:12:59.713 --> 00:13:01.096
as soon as they become available.

00:13:01.096 --> 00:13:04.330
And do your best to read
all the information as well.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.980
If you want to quickly test out
any of these new parts,

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:12.380
then you can press the right bumper
during assembly to initiate an AC test.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:16.730
Or you can just head down into the AC test
area from your Sortie menu.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.763
Once you're here, press the pause button.

00:13:18.763 --> 00:13:23.346
It's in this menu that you can spawn
a variety of enemies to practice against

00:13:23.346 --> 00:13:27.680
without having to worry about incurring
costs from going out on missions.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.663
You can also switch out parts in assembly
and they'll appear here on your

00:13:31.663 --> 00:13:33.280
AC immediately.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:37.130
You can even restock your ammunition
and heal up if needed.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:39.580
AC Testing is an incredible tool.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:42.730
However, in many cases
it might be beneficial for you

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:47.596
to just go out on actual missions instead
and test out your weapons in the field

00:13:47.596 --> 00:13:48.530
for this purpose.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.096
There's the replay missions option.

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:54.996
If you're confident in your abilities,
then by replaying missions,

00:13:54.996 --> 00:13:59.196
you stand to gain additional credits
or a higher rank as well.

00:13:59.196 --> 00:14:03.946
And what's more, some missions have
optional objectives or parts within them.

00:14:03.946 --> 00:14:07.779
So go out there, get some more practice,
earn some more credits

00:14:07.779 --> 00:14:09.796
and see what you can find.

00:14:09.796 --> 00:14:11.046
But when you feel ready,

00:14:11.046 --> 00:14:15.079
you can sortie onto your next mission
and progress in the game.

00:14:15.079 --> 00:14:18.996
Oftentimes, you'll have a choice
of mission and you might want to read

00:14:18.996 --> 00:14:23.796
the mission descriptions and evaluate
how many credits are on offer as well.

00:14:23.796 --> 00:14:27.129
Because you'll need those credits
soon enough, because

00:14:27.129 --> 00:14:31.179
after mission 2, the parts
shop becomes available

00:14:31.179 --> 00:14:34.879
here, you can buy new parts
or sell your old parts.

00:14:34.879 --> 00:14:35.796
And as you complete

00:14:35.796 --> 00:14:39.579
more missions, new parts
will quickly become available in the shop.

00:14:39.579 --> 00:14:42.013
Your available credits can be seen here.

00:14:42.013 --> 00:14:45.396
The price of parts can be seen
here, and buying parts

00:14:45.396 --> 00:14:48.613
will show you a reduction
of your available funds.

00:14:48.613 --> 00:14:51.279
But the most important takeaway is this.

00:14:51.279 --> 00:14:55.096
Don't be afraid of buying new parts
and experimenting here.

00:14:55.096 --> 00:14:58.896
It's absolutely essential
that you get a feel for different parts.

00:14:58.896 --> 00:15:03.129
And most importantly,
parts can always be sold back to the shop

00:15:03.129 --> 00:15:04.996
for the same price you purchased them at. 

00:15:04.996 --> 00:15:09.879
So nothing is ever really lost
in this shopping process.

00:15:09.879 --> 00:15:12.979
Soon we'll go over the process
of constructing an AC,

00:15:12.979 --> 00:15:17.029
but first I want to say that
there's one more way to acquire AC parts,

00:15:17.029 --> 00:15:20.229
and that's through a process
called log hunt.

00:15:20.229 --> 00:15:24.612
After Mission three, you'll be able
to participate in this log hunt program.

00:15:24.612 --> 00:15:28.329
This means that every time you defeat
an enemy in a mission that is marked

00:15:28.329 --> 00:15:33.429
with this battle log icon, you'll gain
progress towards your next Hunter rank,

00:15:33.429 --> 00:15:37.296
at which point
all-mind will reward you with new parts.

00:15:37.296 --> 00:15:40.512
Battle logs
can either be bronze, silver, gold

00:15:40.512 --> 00:15:44.029
or platinum,
with each being worth more than the last.

00:15:44.029 --> 00:15:46.962
So keep a lookout
for these markers in your missions,

00:15:46.962 --> 00:15:51.012
and if you do miss one, consider
replaying that mission to claim it.

00:15:51.012 --> 00:15:55.746
Battle log status will be shown in your
replay mission screen here and here.

00:15:55.746 --> 00:15:59.796
So if it ever says pending
or the icon is grayed out.

00:15:59.796 --> 00:16:00.729
Replay the mission.

00:16:00.729 --> 00:16:04.629
Find that battle log
and complete the mission to claim it.

00:16:04.629 --> 00:16:08.779
Before long, you should start feeling
a lot more confident in your piloting.

00:16:08.779 --> 00:16:12.462
For me, this happened around Mission five,
which was a short mission

00:16:12.462 --> 00:16:16.896
that required that I take out
a Defang student pilot.

00:16:16.896 --> 00:16:18.529
This mission was over fast.

00:16:18.529 --> 00:16:22.446
It wasn't too hard
and it netted me a lot of credits.

00:16:22.446 --> 00:16:26.046
So I replayed this over
and over for a while.

00:16:26.046 --> 00:16:29.929
These frantic
AC fights are great practice, so

00:16:29.929 --> 00:16:33.546
if you're struggling, I highly recommend
you replay this mission.

00:16:33.546 --> 00:16:35.829
Challenge yourself to destroy the enemy.

00:16:35.829 --> 00:16:37.629
AC as quickly as possible.

00:16:37.629 --> 00:16:38.629
Claim your credits.

00:16:38.629 --> 00:16:43.512
Go out and buy a new part to test and
then go back in and take out the enemy.

00:16:43.512 --> 00:16:44.779
AC Again.

00:16:44.779 --> 00:16:48.162
If you get an S rank,
you are doing really well in this mission.

00:16:48.162 --> 00:16:51.612
Before long, you'll be feeling much
more confident with the flow of the game

00:16:51.612 --> 00:16:55.595
and after a few more missions
you'll have enough credits to refine your

00:16:55.595 --> 00:16:59.195
AC into something that you want to pilot.

00:16:59.195 --> 00:17:01.745
And that process of refining a build

00:17:01.745 --> 00:17:04.779
is a huge part
of the joy in Armored Core.

00:17:04.779 --> 00:17:07.929
There's a special sort of satisfaction
that comes with

00:17:07.929 --> 00:17:11.262
putting together builds to perfectly suit
your needs.

00:17:11.262 --> 00:17:16.729
So let's head into AC design
and break down that process.

00:17:16.729 --> 00:17:19.512
As we go through the process of AC design,

00:17:19.512 --> 00:17:23.045
remember, you'll rarely find parts
that are objectively

00:17:23.045 --> 00:17:25.095
better than others in every way.

00:17:25.095 --> 00:17:27.829
Instead, parts are balanced
by being strong

00:17:27.829 --> 00:17:31.179
in some areas and weaker in others.

00:17:31.179 --> 00:17:35.262
If a stat is blue,
that means that stat is an improvement

00:17:35.262 --> 00:17:39.579
over the stat of the part that you
currently have equipped in that slot.

00:17:39.579 --> 00:17:42.429
If it's red,
then that stat is a downgrade.

00:17:42.429 --> 00:17:46.362
It's up to you to decide what stats
you value the most for your build,

00:17:46.362 --> 00:17:51.162
and that's what makes this build process
so fun and personal.

00:17:51.162 --> 00:17:55.245
12 parts
make up an AC assembly for unit parts

00:17:55.245 --> 00:18:00.095
four frame parts, three inner parts,
and an expansion slot.

00:18:00.095 --> 00:18:05.078
When you arrive in the AC design screen,
you can cycle through these 12 categories

00:18:05.078 --> 00:18:08.678
horizontally with your left
and right bumpers, and in the column below

00:18:08.678 --> 00:18:12.395
you'll be able to select the specific part
that you'd like to equip

00:18:12.395 --> 00:18:13.845
from that category.

00:18:13.845 --> 00:18:16.595
Each part has a name, seen here.

00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:20.678
A weapon class
like handgun or bazooka seen here,

00:18:20.678 --> 00:18:23.745
and a written description
that tells you a bit about the weapon.

00:18:23.745 --> 00:18:27.612
Descriptions are often great at describing
what's unique about a weapon at a glance

00:18:27.612 --> 00:18:30.878
without you needing to go deeper
into stats to figure it out.

00:18:30.878 --> 00:18:33.345
For example, this bazooka description
tells us 

00:18:33.345 --> 00:18:35.645
that it deals heavy impact damage

00:18:35.645 --> 00:18:39.495
And if we go back into the part’s
specs section,

00:18:39.495 --> 00:18:43.745
we can confirm that this number is in blue
and has an upwards arrow

00:18:43.745 --> 00:18:48.828
signifying that this weapon indeed
does do a lot more impact damage

00:18:48.828 --> 00:18:51.678
than the assault rifle
we currently have equipped.

00:18:51.678 --> 00:18:55.395
What we currently have equipped
is actually all the way down at the lower

00:18:55.395 --> 00:19:00.345
end of the impact scale
as shown by this little gray marker.

00:19:00.345 --> 00:19:04.545
These five specs
are the simplified specs of each part.

00:19:04.545 --> 00:19:07.928
If you want to look at each part's
detailed specs, you can press

00:19:07.928 --> 00:19:10.778
triangle or Y for an expanded list.

00:19:10.778 --> 00:19:14.228
And if you need any help
figuring out what all these specs do,

00:19:14.228 --> 00:19:18.012
then you can press the Help
button, select contextual help

00:19:18.012 --> 00:19:22.095
and then cycle through for a
more detailed description of each spec.

00:19:22.095 --> 00:19:26.828
If this expanded start screen is
overwhelming to you, don't worry too much.

00:19:26.828 --> 00:19:31.128
Beginners can absolutely get by
with just the simplified start screen.

00:19:31.128 --> 00:19:34.995
So for now,
let's go back to that simplified view.

00:19:34.995 --> 00:19:37.961
Almost all parts have two specs in common.

00:19:37.961 --> 00:19:41.195
They all have a weight
and they all have an EN load.

00:19:41.195 --> 00:19:46.278
The combined weight and EN load
total of all your currently equipped parts

00:19:46.278 --> 00:19:52.128
can be seen on the right here, in a section
that shows your AC’s combined spec total.

00:19:52.128 --> 00:19:54.845
Again,
you can toggle an expanded view of this

00:19:54.845 --> 00:19:58.845
if you like, but the simplified version
is more than enough for now.

00:19:58.845 --> 00:20:01.578
And even then,
what you'll really want to keep an eye on

00:20:01.578 --> 00:20:05.178
the most is your current load
and your current EN load.

00:20:05.178 --> 00:20:09.578
This little gray marker shows
what your current load is at. This red

00:20:09.611 --> 00:20:12.978
or blue bar shows
how the currently selected part

00:20:12.978 --> 00:20:17.328
will affect your current load
and the gray marker with an arrow

00:20:17.328 --> 00:20:20.495
shows the maximum load your AC can handle.

00:20:20.495 --> 00:20:24.128
We'll talk about weight
limit a little bit later, but for now,

00:20:24.128 --> 00:20:29.611
just remember that you generally
do not want to ever go beyond this arrowed marker.

00:20:29.611 --> 00:20:31.778
Weight and EN load are the two

00:20:31.778 --> 00:20:35.628
limiting factors
that help to offset the strength of parts.

00:20:35.628 --> 00:20:36.845
If a part is heavier

00:20:36.845 --> 00:20:41.561
with a high EN load, that means the part
will generally be more powerful.

00:20:41.561 --> 00:20:46.061
But it also means that it will be
more difficult for your AC to carry it.

00:20:46.061 --> 00:20:51.344
If a part is light with a low EN load,
then the part might be somewhat weaker,

00:20:51.344 --> 00:20:55.178
but your AC will more easily
be able to equip it.

00:20:55.178 --> 00:20:59.194
The power and utility of each part
are expressed by the main

00:20:59.194 --> 00:21:02.944
specs situated above their weight
and EN load.

00:21:02.944 --> 00:21:08.228
For weapons, these specs are typically attack
power, impact, and total rounds.

00:21:08.228 --> 00:21:12.428
Attack power determines the damage
dealing performance of each projectile.

00:21:12.428 --> 00:21:15.911
Essentially, it's how much damage
you can do to an enemy's health bar

00:21:15.911 --> 00:21:20.144
impact determines the damage that you do
to an enemy's ACS train.

00:21:20.144 --> 00:21:23.678
The higher your impact,
the more easily you'll be able

00:21:23.678 --> 00:21:27.778
to stagger an enemy
and open them up to direct damage.

00:21:27.844 --> 00:21:31.244
Total rounds are simply the total amount
of ammunition that you're

00:21:31.244 --> 00:21:33.344
bringing into a mission with that weapon.

00:21:33.344 --> 00:21:36.844
This can be relevant
as if you run out of ammunition.

00:21:36.844 --> 00:21:39.844
You'll no longer be able to fire
the weapon.

00:21:39.844 --> 00:21:43.778
Instead, the depleted weapon
will be purged from your AC and

00:21:43.778 --> 00:21:48.278
you'll be forced to fight with your fists
instead, which can still work.

00:21:48.278 --> 00:21:51.394
In addition to these specs, weapon parts
also have

00:21:51.394 --> 00:21:54.378
some icons that tell you
more about the weapon at a glance.

00:21:54.378 --> 00:21:57.094
For example, the fourth slot will tell you
if this weapon

00:21:57.094 --> 00:22:00.094
affects a particular part of the enemy
craft.

00:22:00.128 --> 00:22:04.028
The napalm launcher, for example,
can inflict a status effect

00:22:04.028 --> 00:22:07.028
that will cause the enemy to be staggered
more easily.

00:22:07.028 --> 00:22:11.194
The third icon represents
whether a weapon is single shot or whether

00:22:11.194 --> 00:22:16.027
it needs to be reloaded, or if it doesn't
need to be reloaded and will overheat.

00:22:16.027 --> 00:22:21.244
Instead, if a weapon can overheat,
the progress towards overheat can be seen

00:22:21.244 --> 00:22:26.211
accumulating here around your lock
on, if possible, keep an eye on the spart

00:22:26.211 --> 00:22:30.327
and space out your shots
to allow your weapon to cool.

00:22:30.394 --> 00:22:33.977
This will avoid putting your weapon
into an overheat state.

00:22:33.977 --> 00:22:37.177
If a weapon is in an overheat state,
then you can't fire it

00:22:37.177 --> 00:22:39.827
and you just have to wait for it
to cool down.

00:22:39.827 --> 00:22:44.677
And the second icon corresponds to
the type of weapon seen up here as well.

00:22:44.677 --> 00:22:48.094
And the first icon tells you
the damage type of the weapon.

00:22:48.094 --> 00:22:51.727
So there are three types of damage
that your weapons can deal in.

00:22:51.727 --> 00:22:56.144
Armor, of course,
six kinetic energy and explosive.

00:22:56.144 --> 00:22:58.594
First, let's talk kinetic damage.

00:22:58.594 --> 00:23:01.327
This is damage done
with physical projectiles.

00:23:01.327 --> 00:23:06.011
Most common in weapons like the assault
rifle, the machine gun, or shotguns.

00:23:06.011 --> 00:23:09.694
Kinetic weapons are typically better
at close or medium range.

00:23:09.694 --> 00:23:14.194
They typically fire quite fast
and they generally also have a

00:23:14.194 --> 00:23:18.044
higher direct hit adjustment
spec on average, which means

00:23:18.044 --> 00:23:22.211
they're a great option for dealing damage
while an enemy is staggered.

00:23:22.211 --> 00:23:24.561
The second type of damage is energy
damage.

00:23:24.561 --> 00:23:30.261
This is further split into three
more types laser plasma and pulse.

00:23:30.261 --> 00:23:32.594
Laser weapons fire, straight blue beams.

00:23:32.594 --> 00:23:36.877
Plasma weapons are purple and create
an AOE explosion on impact. 

00:23:36.877 --> 00:23:38.327
and pulse weaponry

00:23:38.327 --> 00:23:43.394
Fire bubble beams that are great at
wearing down pulse defenses.

00:23:43.394 --> 00:23:47.810
On average, though, energy weapons
fire slowly and are typically better

00:23:47.810 --> 00:23:52.210
at long range with high attack power,
but low impact.

00:23:52.210 --> 00:23:56.377
So use these to capitalize on an enemy's
broken guard.

00:23:56.377 --> 00:23:59.227
Don't always rely on them to break it.

00:23:59.227 --> 00:24:01.877
The third type of damage is explosive
damage

00:24:01.877 --> 00:24:05.744
typically dealt by bazookas,
grenades, and missiles.

00:24:05.744 --> 00:24:08.710
Explosive projectiles often deal
the same amount of damage

00:24:08.710 --> 00:24:13.277
regardless of range and often create
an AOP explosion to boot.

00:24:13.277 --> 00:24:18.560
What's more, weapons with explosive damage
have high impact and attack power specs.

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:23.777
However, this is offset
by slow firing rates and a lot of recoil.

00:24:23.777 --> 00:24:27.610
They're a great tool to have
for breaking open enemy guards though,

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:30.760
and most builds are well served by having

00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:34.010
at least one explosive weapon equipped.

00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:35.927
So those are the three types of damage.

00:24:35.927 --> 00:24:39.527
But naturally,
there are three types of defense as well.

00:24:39.527 --> 00:24:43.727
If you're stuck on a boss or enemies,
consider what their defensive stats

00:24:43.727 --> 00:24:48.944
or weaknesses might be and experiment
with different types of weapons.

00:24:48.944 --> 00:24:51.677
Before I move on from weapons,
I'd like to mention

00:24:51.677 --> 00:24:54.677
melee weapons and pulse shields as well.

00:24:54.710 --> 00:24:58.127
Melee weapons can only be equipped
to the left arm slot

00:24:58.127 --> 00:25:02.860
and pulse shields can only be equipped
to the left back slot.

00:25:02.860 --> 00:25:07.177
We've talked about melee weapons already,
but note that they have a main spec

00:25:07.177 --> 00:25:11.210
called Consecutive Hits, which lets
you know how many times

00:25:11.210 --> 00:25:16.127
the melee weapon can strike
with repeated taps of L2.

00:25:16.127 --> 00:25:20.027
As for pulse shields, I probably wouldn't
recommend them for a beginner

00:25:20.027 --> 00:25:25.027
as using them properly requires
quite a bit of timing and finesse.

00:25:25.027 --> 00:25:28.727
That said, if you do want to equip
one note that their main specs are 

00:25:28.727 --> 00:25:33.093
damage mitigation, impact dampening,
and deployment range. 

00:25:33.093 --> 00:25:36.127
damage mitigation is essentially the percentage of damage

00:25:36.127 --> 00:25:38.577
that the shield will block, while it’s active.

00:25:38.577 --> 00:25:43.327
Impacts dampening is a mechanic
that determines your initial guard window.

00:25:43.327 --> 00:25:44.377
When shields are deployed,

00:25:44.377 --> 00:25:48.760
there's this little brief moment
where you can block more incoming damage.

00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:54.277
So blocks should be timed ideally
to correspond with incoming attacks.

00:25:54.277 --> 00:25:57.760
But be aware that this will overheat
your shield more quickly

00:25:57.760 --> 00:26:01.060
so you can't just repeatedly tap
it too many times.

00:26:01.060 --> 00:26:06.110
Lastly, deployment range is a value
that determines the size of your shield.

00:26:06.110 --> 00:26:09.160
Next,
we have the full frame parts of the AC.

00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:10.393
Let's start with the head.

00:26:10.393 --> 00:26:13.727
Head parts are unique
in that they determine the power

00:26:13.727 --> 00:26:16.960
and range of your scan function,
but beyond that,

00:26:16.960 --> 00:26:22.093
their main specs are AP, attitude
stability, and system recovery.

00:26:22.093 --> 00:26:26.310
AP are your armor points, your health basically.

00:26:26.310 --> 00:26:28.243
Attitude stability contributes

00:26:28.243 --> 00:26:31.693
towards the maximum amount of stagger damage
that you can absorb.

00:26:31.693 --> 00:26:35.810
So a higher value means
it'll be harder for an enemy to strain

00:26:35.810 --> 00:26:39.860
your attitude control system
and knock you off balance.

00:26:39.860 --> 00:26:44.026
And finally, system recovery determines
how fast you will recover

00:26:44.026 --> 00:26:48.560
from status effects inflicted by things
like fire or electricity.

00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:50.110
Next, the core part.

00:26:50.110 --> 00:26:50.893
This is the part

00:26:50.893 --> 00:26:55.243
that will typically contribute
the most AP and attitude to your build.

00:26:55.243 --> 00:26:59.893
It's also typically the heaviest uniquely,
though the core part also has a stat

00:26:59.893 --> 00:27:04.693
called generator Output Adjust,
which is a value that determines

00:27:04.693 --> 00:27:09.610
how effective your generator parts
will be at fulfilling your energy needs.

00:27:09.610 --> 00:27:14.360
But we'll get into energy
and generators a little bit later.

00:27:14.360 --> 00:27:16.060
And then there are the arms.

00:27:16.060 --> 00:27:16.476
Arms.

00:27:16.476 --> 00:27:20.110
Give AP, of course,
But the unique specs determine

00:27:20.110 --> 00:27:24.376
your arm load limits
and your level of firearm specialization.

00:27:24.376 --> 00:27:28.243
Armload limits can come into play
when your arms are carrying extremely

00:27:28.243 --> 00:27:29.410
heavy weaponry.

00:27:29.410 --> 00:27:31.543
If you're holding weapons
that are too heavy,

00:27:31.543 --> 00:27:34.810
you'll get this warning on the right,
which means you'll need to equip

00:27:34.810 --> 00:27:38.710
lighter weaponry or choose arms
with a heavier load limit.

00:27:38.710 --> 00:27:42.076
Finally, there's firearm specialization,
which improves

00:27:42.076 --> 00:27:43.993
target tracking performance.

00:27:43.993 --> 00:27:47.059
If you find your shots are missing,
your target a lot.

00:27:47.059 --> 00:27:52.276
Consider selecting armor parts
that have higher firearm specialization.

00:27:52.276 --> 00:27:55.276
Finally, and most importantly,
we have the leg parts.

00:27:55.276 --> 00:28:01.093
And this might just be the most important
part in your AC’s entire assembly.

00:28:01.093 --> 00:28:02.376
Let me explain.

00:28:02.376 --> 00:28:06.576
So leg parts contribute
AP and attitude stability

00:28:06.576 --> 00:28:10.809
like all your other frame parts, but
they unique in that they are responsible

00:28:10.809 --> 00:28:15.909
for carrying the combined
weight of everything else on your AC.

00:28:15.909 --> 00:28:20.709
Thus, the most defining spec
is this their load limit.

00:28:20.709 --> 00:28:24.259
This value changes
this arrowed marker over here

00:28:24.259 --> 00:28:26.976
which determines the maximum weight
you can carry.

00:28:26.976 --> 00:28:31.726
And it's the marker that you never want
to exceed when building your AC.

00:28:31.726 --> 00:28:36.193
Generally, the closer you can get your AC
to this load limit, the better.

00:28:36.193 --> 00:28:39.976
Though I will point out that
the further back you go from this marker,

00:28:39.976 --> 00:28:43.659
the lighter your AC will be
and it will grant a slight

00:28:43.659 --> 00:28:47.076
increase to your boost speed as a result.

00:28:47.076 --> 00:28:52.309
But the really unique thing about
legs is up here, and that's their type.

00:28:52.309 --> 00:28:58.176
There are four types of leg:
bipedal, reverse jointed, quadruped legs

00:28:58.176 --> 00:29:03.009
and tank treads
Each come in heavy or light variants.

00:29:03.009 --> 00:29:07.476
But it's the type of leg you choose
that plays a massive part

00:29:07.476 --> 00:29:10.542
in how your AC will control.

00:29:10.542 --> 00:29:13.159
Biped legs are your jack of all trades.

00:29:13.159 --> 00:29:15.576
They're certainly a safe
bet for new players

00:29:15.576 --> 00:29:19.509
and they're all you have access to
at the beginning of the game.

00:29:19.509 --> 00:29:23.026
Before long, though,
you'll unlock these reverse joints.

00:29:23.026 --> 00:29:27.042
Reverse joints are still bipedal legs,
but they're unique in that

00:29:27.042 --> 00:29:30.459
they have unparalleled
jumping abilities in gameplay.

00:29:30.459 --> 00:29:34.876
This means that your jump will propel you
further into the air, and it also means

00:29:34.876 --> 00:29:39.159
that your quick boost will fling you
further to the side while you're grounded.

00:29:39.159 --> 00:29:42.309
Consider reverse joints
if you need to be more airborne

00:29:42.309 --> 00:29:46.176
or more evasive,
but note that you'll generally be more

00:29:46.176 --> 00:29:50.509
easy to knock off balance
if you're ever hit with these legs.

00:29:50.509 --> 00:29:54.576
One of the drawbacks to all bipedal legs
is that they don't absorb

00:29:54.576 --> 00:29:58.809
recoil whenever you fire
heavy weaponry or burst weaponry.

00:29:58.809 --> 00:30:03.076
Notice how I'm pausing in the air
when I fire these sorts of weapons?

00:30:03.076 --> 00:30:05.292
That's because of my biped legs.

00:30:05.292 --> 00:30:10.626
And while it's absolutely still viable
to use weapons like these with biped legs,

00:30:10.626 --> 00:30:16.009
this pause can definitely get you
destroyed, If you fire at the wrong moment.

00:30:16.009 --> 00:30:19.126
However, that recoil is not as impactful

00:30:19.126 --> 00:30:23.926
with the other two classes of leg
which are quadruped and tank treads.

00:30:23.926 --> 00:30:28.092
Quadruped and tank treads
can absorb recoil from heavy or burst

00:30:28.092 --> 00:30:31.609
weaponry, allowing you to fire them
while you're moving.

00:30:31.609 --> 00:30:35.259
Though it's worth noting that quads do
slow down slightly

00:30:35.259 --> 00:30:38.375
while firing, while tanks are uninhibited.

00:30:38.375 --> 00:30:39.642
Completely.

00:30:39.642 --> 00:30:45.125
This ability to hover is what sets
quadrupeds apart from tank treads.

00:30:45.125 --> 00:30:48.259
Once you're airborne, all you need to do
is press the jump button again

00:30:48.259 --> 00:30:51.459
with X or A to hover in the air.

00:30:51.459 --> 00:30:55.009
Pressing jump a third time
will drop you out of this mode.

00:30:55.009 --> 00:30:58.725
While you're in it, you can still dodge
and fire your weaponry, though

00:30:58.725 --> 00:30:59.592
you are slow

00:30:59.592 --> 00:31:04.175
and you'll need to return to the ground
to make substantial energy gains.

00:31:04.175 --> 00:31:05.742
The biggest advantage

00:31:05.742 --> 00:31:09.759
of flying like this is for maintaining
additional range from enemies.

00:31:09.759 --> 00:31:14.409
And just in the fact that it often gives
you a straight line of sight at enemies

00:31:14.409 --> 00:31:17.475
without any environmental clutter
getting in your way.

00:31:17.475 --> 00:31:20.742
It's also amazing against sudden enemies
that don't have attacks

00:31:20.742 --> 00:31:21.675
that can reach you.

00:31:21.675 --> 00:31:26.775
So consider keeping a set of quadruped
legs on hand in case you need them.

00:31:26.775 --> 00:31:31.059
They can be a really powerful situational
tool to have at your disposal

00:31:31.059 --> 00:31:33.209
thanks to their hover ability.

00:31:33.209 --> 00:31:34.275
With tank treads,

00:31:34.275 --> 00:31:38.292
On the other hand, your booster part
is actually removed from your

00:31:38.292 --> 00:31:44.025
AC assembly entirely as the tank treads
come with their own in-built boosters.

00:31:44.025 --> 00:31:48.942
With some exceptions, flight
isn't typically a strong point of most

00:31:48.942 --> 00:31:50.075
tank treads.

00:31:50.075 --> 00:31:54.009
Tank treads are more about grounded
movement and operating.

00:31:54.009 --> 00:31:57.108
These really feels like
driving a wheeled vehicle

00:31:57.108 --> 00:32:00.308
where the direction
you're facing really matters.

00:32:00.308 --> 00:32:04.175
That said, you can still quick boost
while grounded, which will instantly

00:32:04.175 --> 00:32:08.925
change your direction if needed and propel
you into a temporary drift state.

00:32:09.008 --> 00:32:12.158
Slower treads will also benefit
from making frequent

00:32:12.158 --> 00:32:15.408
use of the assault boost ability
to cover distance.

00:32:15.492 --> 00:32:18.225
At the end of the day,
though, tank treads are really designed

00:32:18.225 --> 00:32:21.875
to carry an enormous load
and it's generally

00:32:21.875 --> 00:32:25.925
a good idea to load your tank
with the most devastating weaponry

00:32:25.925 --> 00:32:29.925
and the most resilient frame parts
you can carry.

00:32:29.925 --> 00:32:35.442
The next three parts of your AC are its
inside parts, which consist of the booster.

00:32:35.442 --> 00:32:41.375
The FCS and the generator. Booster parts
are most defined by their thrust,

00:32:41.375 --> 00:32:45.642
their upward thrust and their quick boost
thrust specs.

00:32:45.642 --> 00:32:51.442
Your basic thrust value is what determines
your default speed while gliding and flying.

00:32:51.442 --> 00:32:56.058
An AC with a high default
speed will naturally be quite avoidant

00:32:56.058 --> 00:32:56.892
without you needing

00:32:56.892 --> 00:33:01.508
to take any particularly evasive maneuvers
which you might consider useful.

00:33:01.508 --> 00:33:04.608
If you want to focus on things
other than dodging.

00:33:04.608 --> 00:33:07.008
Your upward
thrust is exactly what it sounds like.

00:33:07.008 --> 00:33:11.475
This value determines how powerful
your upward trajectory will be.

00:33:11.475 --> 00:33:15.008
Being in the air can help you
to avoid explosions on the ground,

00:33:15.008 --> 00:33:18.342
and it also allows you
to get a better angle on your enemies.

00:33:18.342 --> 00:33:23.625
So consider this spec
especially relevant for sudden encounters.

00:33:23.625 --> 00:33:26.891
And then there's your quick boost thrust,
which determines

00:33:26.891 --> 00:33:30.725
how fast your thrust will be
when your quick boost is activated.

00:33:30.725 --> 00:33:34.208
This expanded view actually
shows a lot more quick boost values

00:33:34.208 --> 00:33:38.175
that you should also consider,
but generally you should only select

00:33:38.175 --> 00:33:39.375
for quick boost thrust.

00:33:39.375 --> 00:33:40.775
If you find yourself

00:33:40.775 --> 00:33:45.675
facing an enemy that you think requires
a lot of manual dodging.

00:33:45.675 --> 00:33:48.975
Another important stat is hidden
in the expanded stat screen,

00:33:48.975 --> 00:33:52.758
and that's quick
boost reload ideal weight spec.

00:33:52.758 --> 00:33:58.241
If your total weight rises above this
value, your AC will have its quick boosts.

00:33:58.241 --> 00:34:01.541
reload time progressively penalized

00:34:01.541 --> 00:34:04.308
Quick boosts and flight require energy.

00:34:04.308 --> 00:34:07.425
So naturally
we should talk about the generator next

00:34:07.425 --> 00:34:11.708
because it's this part that determines
the nature of your energy bar.

00:34:11.708 --> 00:34:14.708
The generators
main specs are its EN capacity,

00:34:14.708 --> 00:34:18.408
its EN recharge and its supply recovery.

00:34:18.408 --> 00:34:23.325
EN capacity simply determines the maximum
amount of energy in your energy bar.

00:34:23.325 --> 00:34:26.975
An AC with a higher
EN capacity will be able to perform

00:34:26.975 --> 00:34:30.525
more actions before this bar is depleted.

00:34:30.525 --> 00:34:34.825
However, it's also important
to take into account your EN recharge rate

00:34:34.825 --> 00:34:38.508
as this determines
how quickly your energy will recover.

00:34:38.508 --> 00:34:41.858
An AC with a higher recharge
rate will be able to spend

00:34:41.858 --> 00:34:45.458
less time
recovering and more time doing actions.

00:34:45.458 --> 00:34:47.408
Then there's supply recovery,

00:34:47.408 --> 00:34:50.658
which determines
how quickly your generator will recover.

00:34:50.658 --> 00:34:53.108
If you fully deplete your energy bar.

00:34:53.108 --> 00:34:55.874
Ideally, you'll never fully
deplete your energy bar,

00:34:55.874 --> 00:35:00.108
but sometimes that's necessary
to avoid attacks and high supply

00:35:00.108 --> 00:35:05.208
recovery will get you back to the action
without being punished too hard.

00:35:05.208 --> 00:35:08.224
Finally, unlike every other part,
the generator doesn't

00:35:08.224 --> 00:35:10.458
actually have an EN load.

00:35:10.458 --> 00:35:11.974
It has EN output.

00:35:11.974 --> 00:35:15.541
So it's the generator
that's responsible for supporting the 

00:35:15.541 --> 00:35:17.858
EN load of the rest of your system.

00:35:17.858 --> 00:35:21.824
Your total EN load can be seen here
on the right, and the gray marker

00:35:21.824 --> 00:35:25.691
represents the combined EN load
of all your currently equipped parts.

00:35:25.691 --> 00:35:28.774
That red or blue bar determines
how that EN load

00:35:28.774 --> 00:35:32.141
will change depending on the part
you have selected.

00:35:32.141 --> 00:35:35.474
And the arrowed marker is your maximum
EN capacity

00:35:35.474 --> 00:35:39.074
as defined by your generators
and output stat.

00:35:39.074 --> 00:35:42.424
Basically,
if you're exceeding your maximum EN load,

00:35:42.424 --> 00:35:46.274
you'll see red here
and that means you either need to switch

00:35:46.274 --> 00:35:52.274
to more energy efficient parts or choose
a generator with a higher EN output.

00:35:52.274 --> 00:35:55.174
The last part we need to go over
is the FCS part,

00:35:55.174 --> 00:35:59.624
which is the biggest contributor
to your aiming accuracy.

00:35:59.624 --> 00:36:02.074
You might have noticed
when you lock onto enemies,

00:36:02.074 --> 00:36:06.757
your aim is actually determined
by this little reticle within the lock on.

00:36:06.757 --> 00:36:11.474
When it's red, you're considered in range
and your non homing projectiles

00:36:11.474 --> 00:36:13.024
should hit their mark.

00:36:13.024 --> 00:36:18.574
Keyword there, though, is should because
this little reticle isn't always on point.

00:36:18.574 --> 00:36:22.324
Sometimes it will waver,
sometimes it will lag behind.

00:36:22.324 --> 00:36:26.974
And it's this behavior
that is determined by the FCS part.

00:36:26.974 --> 00:36:31.174
FCS parts have three main specs:
their close range assist

00:36:31.174 --> 00:36:34.574
medium range assist and long range assist.

00:36:34.574 --> 00:36:37.841
Close range assist determines
how good your reticle will be

00:36:37.841 --> 00:36:41.807
at tracking enemies
within the 130 meter range.

00:36:41.807 --> 00:36:45.407
Medium range determines
how good tracking will be between 130

00:36:45.407 --> 00:36:48.407
and 260 meters and long range determines

00:36:48.407 --> 00:36:52.057
how good tracking will be beyond 260
meters.

00:36:52.057 --> 00:36:56.141
Pay special attention to distance markers
during combat

00:36:56.141 --> 00:37:02.024
and try to stay within the optimal range
for your FCS and your weapon.

00:37:02.024 --> 00:37:07.657
Missile tracking is separate from the FCS,
but the FCS does determine

00:37:07.657 --> 00:37:13.691
how fast you can acquire a missile lock
and how fast your lock capabilities are.

00:37:13.691 --> 00:37:17.657
So this is a factor
to consider for your build.

00:37:17.657 --> 00:37:20.407
And that's the basics
of everything in your assembly.

00:37:20.407 --> 00:37:24.707
And if it sounds like a lot,
well, you're not wrong, but rest assured

00:37:24.707 --> 00:37:28.957
that it will start to make sense
as you jump in and experiment with things.

00:37:28.957 --> 00:37:33.257
So let's try
and put together a unique build now.

00:37:33.257 --> 00:37:37.124
And while yours might be different
from this build, I'll show you the order

00:37:37.124 --> 00:37:41.107
that I generally prefer
to put things together.

00:37:41.107 --> 00:37:44.240
One of the most straightforward ways
to get started with a build

00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:48.440
is to first decide on which FCS
you should use.

00:37:48.440 --> 00:37:51.307
That's
because this forces you to decide early

00:37:51.307 --> 00:37:55.757
whether you want to build something
for close, medium or long range,

00:37:55.757 --> 00:37:59.290
or whether you want something
that's just decent at every range.

00:37:59.290 --> 00:38:02.690
Having an idea in mind helps
when getting started.

00:38:02.690 --> 00:38:08.240
So let's aim for a close range
build and choose a close range part.

00:38:08.240 --> 00:38:16.057
The focus I want to go for
is this: the FCS-G2 / P10SLT

00:38:16.057 --> 00:38:19.057
It has good performance
at close to medium range

00:38:19.057 --> 00:38:22.940
and it comes with the added
benefit of quick missile lock time,

00:38:22.940 --> 00:38:26.357
which is great
as we'll be using missiles as well.

00:38:26.357 --> 00:38:31.757
So next, let's choose a good close
range, arm weapon to suit our FCS.

00:38:31.757 --> 00:38:34.657
Expanded specs screens
reveal optimal ranges

00:38:34.657 --> 00:38:39.757
for firing each weapon
and the one for the MG-014 Ludlow

00:38:39.757 --> 00:38:42.674
 reveals
that it's a great close range option.

00:38:42.674 --> 00:38:44.657
So let's equip two of them.

00:38:44.657 --> 00:38:46.007
One for each arm.

00:38:46.007 --> 00:38:49.040
What we’re using now is called a double trigger
build.

00:38:49.040 --> 00:38:52.490
Meaning
you'll be dual firing these machine guns

00:38:52.490 --> 00:38:54.973
at once with both of your triggers.

00:38:54.973 --> 00:38:55.840
The Ludlow's

00:38:55.840 --> 00:39:00.140
description also specifically calls out
that it's great in dual trigger builds.

00:39:00.140 --> 00:39:03.257
This is why reading descriptions
can be so useful.

00:39:03.257 --> 00:39:06.607
As mentioned before, the description
on our FCS revealed

00:39:06.607 --> 00:39:09.707
that it's principally designed
to reduce missile lock time,

00:39:09.707 --> 00:39:12.907
which means that our missiles
will also be a very effective tool.

00:39:12.907 --> 00:39:17.240
So let's equip two sets of those
on our back and all of a sudden we have

00:39:17.240 --> 00:39:22.640
a build that is deadly at close range
and with long range missiles as well.

00:39:22.640 --> 00:39:23.707
Looking good.

00:39:23.707 --> 00:39:26.257
The next decision I like to make is legs.

00:39:26.257 --> 00:39:30.523
You have to ask
what would suit a close range build

00:39:30.523 --> 00:39:34.340
while you could go light
and avoid taking damage entirely.

00:39:34.340 --> 00:39:38.657
But as a beginner, you're
probably going to get hit a lot anyway, so

00:39:38.657 --> 00:39:40.190
might as well go with something heavy.

00:39:40.190 --> 00:39:45.107
For now, let's go with the Tian Qiang
bipedal legs. As these

00:39:45.107 --> 00:39:50.507
give us a high load limit to play with
while we select our other parts.

00:39:50.507 --> 00:39:54.973
Having a high load limit makes it
so much easier to put together an AC.

00:39:54.973 --> 00:40:00.140
I can confidently select heavier parts now
and by intentionally selecting

00:40:00.140 --> 00:40:03.907
for heavy weights.
I can kind of just trust that

00:40:03.907 --> 00:40:07.057
the other specs
will naturally be quite good.

00:40:07.057 --> 00:40:10.190
Another way to quickly put together
a build is to buy parts

00:40:10.190 --> 00:40:13.273
that just exist within a family of parts.

00:40:13.273 --> 00:40:17.840
Most parts will have keywords like VP
or Melander

00:40:17.840 --> 00:40:20.690
as well as a company logo
that can help you

00:40:20.690 --> 00:40:24.223
ascertain the family of parts
that they exist within.

00:40:24.223 --> 00:40:27.456
For example, buying all of Schneider's
Nachtreiher

00:40:27.456 --> 00:40:31.156
parts will make your build
very fast and great in the air.

00:40:31.156 --> 00:40:35.473
Whereas buying all of Dafeng's Tian Qiang parts

00:40:35.473 --> 00:40:39.340
will naturally make you slower
but very tanky.

00:40:39.340 --> 00:40:42.890
So by buying all of the parts in a family,
you can easily

00:40:42.890 --> 00:40:46.806
get a good idea of the type of AC
those parts are moving you towards.

00:40:46.806 --> 00:40:51.606
And while you're definitely encouraged
to mix and match, buying all the parts in

00:40:51.606 --> 00:40:55.023
the family is kind of a guarantee
that they'll work well together,

00:40:55.040 --> 00:40:58.790
which might be a welcoming thing
to many beginners.

00:40:58.790 --> 00:41:01.840
Because I've replayed Mission
five so many times,

00:41:01.840 --> 00:41:05.440
I have over a million credits,
so I'm going to use these

00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:10.123
to buy every frame part in Dafeng’s
heavyweight family of parts.

00:41:10.123 --> 00:41:12.856
If you don't have enough credits
here, consider

00:41:12.856 --> 00:41:16.306
replacing missions
or selling parts that you don't need.

00:41:16.306 --> 00:41:19.940
And if you can't afford the same parts
that I'm buying, don't worry.

00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:24.856
Consider parts to be a goal to work
towards and just see if you can get by.

00:41:24.856 --> 00:41:28.390
In the meantime, next, let's choose
Boosters.

00:41:28.390 --> 00:41:31.873
Manually dodging with a quick boost
can be a lot of extra

00:41:31.873 --> 00:41:37.056
input for a beginner, so let's just select
for a high thrust stat instead.

00:41:37.056 --> 00:41:40.989
This will enable us to move
at a high speed by default

00:41:40.989 --> 00:41:44.856
and we should just naturally avoid
a lot of attacks this way.

00:41:44.856 --> 00:41:49.256
Luckily, the BST-G2/PO4

00:41:49.256 --> 00:41:51.639
 is perfect for those needs.

00:41:51.639 --> 00:41:54.139
Next, I like to choose a generator.

00:41:54.139 --> 00:41:58.756
Now generators can get pretty heavy,
but since we have those high load

00:41:58.756 --> 00:42:03.639
bearing legs, we might as well just choose
the heaviest generator we can find.

00:42:03.639 --> 00:42:07.339
This generator,
the Ling-Tai, gives us a reduction

00:42:07.339 --> 00:42:11.839
in our EN capacity,
but notice it's only a slight reduction

00:42:11.839 --> 00:42:17.706
considering the dramatic increase
in our EN recharge and supply recovery.

00:42:17.706 --> 00:42:21.039
I'd say this is a very welcome trade off,

00:42:21.039 --> 00:42:23.623
so in the end
you should have something like this,

00:42:23.623 --> 00:42:29.289
a close range AC with an extremely high
AP and defensive performance.

00:42:29.289 --> 00:42:30.006
We're not done

00:42:30.006 --> 00:42:34.006
because once you have a build,
you should take a moment to review things.

00:42:34.006 --> 00:42:37.506
The most important thing to look at
is your current load.

00:42:37.506 --> 00:42:38.206
A good goal

00:42:38.206 --> 00:42:41.856
is to try and get as close to your weight
limit as possible without exceeding it.

00:42:41.856 --> 00:42:45.606
So if you have a ton of space
free at this final stage,

00:42:45.606 --> 00:42:49.389
it means you might want to go back
and put on some heavier parts.

00:42:49.389 --> 00:42:52.123
Alternatively,
if you're nowhere near your load limit,

00:42:52.123 --> 00:42:56.739
you might want to go back to your leg
selection and choose lighter load bearing

00:42:56.739 --> 00:43:01.989
legs as that would confer benefits by
bringing you closer to your weight limit.

00:43:01.989 --> 00:43:05.172
All that said, don't worry
too much about being super close

00:43:05.172 --> 00:43:08.589
to your weight limit,
even though I have some space here.

00:43:08.589 --> 00:43:11.806
I'm happy with that too,
because space means I'll be able

00:43:11.806 --> 00:43:15.906
to quickly switch to heavier weapons
if the mission requires it

00:43:15.906 --> 00:43:20.589
without changing any of my other parts,
which is really convenient.

00:43:20.589 --> 00:43:21.639
Speaking of weight,

00:43:21.639 --> 00:43:25.922
consider expanding the stat screen
on your booster here and check 

00:43:25.922 --> 00:43:27.522
that your total load

00:43:27.522 --> 00:43:28.606
doesn't exceed your

00:43:28.606 --> 00:43:31.956
ideal weight
spec on your booster by too much.

00:43:31.956 --> 00:43:33.589
Again, the more you exceed

00:43:33.589 --> 00:43:37.872
this value, the slower
you'll be able to quick boost repeatedly.

00:43:37.872 --> 00:43:41.089
Last check your ACS maximum EN load.

00:43:41.089 --> 00:43:43.456
Like with weight,
it's important to be under

00:43:43.456 --> 00:43:47.506
and as close to your ideal
EN load as possible.

00:43:47.506 --> 00:43:51.189
If you feel like you've settled
into a really optimal build,

00:43:51.189 --> 00:43:55.689
then it's often a great idea
to head into the AC data screen.

00:43:55.689 --> 00:44:00.739
Here you can name your AC
and save this build for future use.

00:44:00.739 --> 00:44:04.689
This is a great way to get some personal
attachment to the build that you're using.

00:44:04.689 --> 00:44:08.856
And also in a practical sense,
having multiple builds on hand

00:44:08.856 --> 00:44:12.672
can help you to quickly adapt
to different situations.

00:44:12.672 --> 00:44:17.406
You can also try and copy enemy
AC presets over in this tab

00:44:17.406 --> 00:44:20.172
as long as you have all their parts
available.

00:44:20.172 --> 00:44:25.039
Finally, consider stockpiling a few back
up parts before you go out into missions.

00:44:25.039 --> 00:44:27.939
This will allow you to switch up
your assembly mid mission,

00:44:27.939 --> 00:44:30.605
which can be extremely useful. 

00:44:30.605 --> 00:44:32.205
Me, personally,

00:44:32.205 --> 00:44:34.489
I'm going to buy two bazookas

00:44:34.489 --> 00:44:38.655
because you never know
when you might need a bazooka or two.

00:44:38.655 --> 00:44:41.105
The first mission
that new players are kind of

00:44:41.105 --> 00:44:44.939
likely to get stuck on
is this Operation Warp Climber.

00:44:45.005 --> 00:44:49.572
So I'm going to use this mission
to show off a few more advanced mechanics.

00:44:49.572 --> 00:44:53.239
Our first objective
is to take out the Gatling guns over here.

00:44:53.239 --> 00:44:56.105
Now, while objective markers show
you your goal,

00:44:56.105 --> 00:44:59.555
you don't always have to take the straight
route to get there.

00:44:59.555 --> 00:45:00.072
For example,

00:45:00.072 --> 00:45:01.905
if we go straight,
there will have to go through

00:45:01.905 --> 00:45:06.139
a battlefield and straight into Gatling
gunfire, which is not the best idea.

00:45:06.139 --> 00:45:07.989
So instead, since our build

00:45:07.989 --> 00:45:11.772
is a little bit on the slower side,
let's take the scenic route.

00:45:11.772 --> 00:45:15.605
The tank is still shooting us,
but by listening for warning signs

00:45:15.605 --> 00:45:20.089
and staying in the air to avoid explosions
on the ground, we can reduce

00:45:20.089 --> 00:45:21.572
damage taken here.

00:45:32.255 --> 00:45:35.689
Next we go over the ramparts,
firing our weaponry on the way.

00:45:35.689 --> 00:45:37.572
Assault boost keeps us fast enough

00:45:37.572 --> 00:45:41.322
and tanky enough to avoid the snipers
aiming at us.

00:45:41.322 --> 00:45:44.589
And by tapping us
end to end my assault boost,

00:45:44.589 --> 00:45:47.472
I can maintain momentum and quickly regain

00:45:47.472 --> 00:45:51.705
energy on the ground.

00:45:51.705 --> 00:45:53.255
By setting up a flanking run.

00:45:53.255 --> 00:45:56.755
I can take out the Gatling guns
without having to stop.

00:46:01.188 --> 00:46:03.105
Next, listen for warning sounds.

00:46:03.105 --> 00:46:04.455
As you go through the city,

00:46:04.455 --> 00:46:08.688
your eyes will basically tell you
when you're at risk of getting hit.

00:46:08.688 --> 00:46:12.522
We can use the environment for cover
and even use our compass

00:46:12.522 --> 00:46:16.455
at the bottom here
to locate any nearby enemies.

00:46:16.455 --> 00:46:19.872
There are quite a few enemy
empties in the city, but

00:46:19.872 --> 00:46:25.138
directional markers will let you know
where an enemy has fired at you from.

00:46:30.222 --> 00:46:31.488
This marker lets me know that

00:46:31.488 --> 00:46:37.205
there's one coming up right behind me.

00:46:37.205 --> 00:46:38.538
Repair kits heal

00:46:38.538 --> 00:46:40.722
A flat 4000 AP.

00:46:40.722 --> 00:46:43.538
You should always try to use them
after you've taken

00:46:43.538 --> 00:46:46.838
4000 damage to make sure
you get the full benefit from it.

00:46:46.838 --> 00:46:50.322
But it's also valuable to stay topped up
so you don't have to heal

00:46:50.322 --> 00:46:53.505
in the middle of a fight instead.

00:46:53.505 --> 00:46:56.288
Our next objective is the BAUS tetrapod.

00:46:56.288 --> 00:46:58.638
It's hidden in a nook under the city.

00:46:58.638 --> 00:47:01.272
Let's get to it.

00:47:01.272 --> 00:47:02.238
There's the tetrapod.

00:47:02.238 --> 00:47:06.072
And because it's a single imposing enemy,
it's probably a good idea

00:47:06.072 --> 00:47:10.005
to toggle on our target
lock with R3 before we get started.

00:47:10.005 --> 00:47:14.138
When fighting enemies, it's important to
keep in mind your weapons effective range.

00:47:14.138 --> 00:47:15.371
This is something that you should try

00:47:15.371 --> 00:47:18.971
and memorize in the garage
before heading into battle.

00:47:18.971 --> 00:47:22.088
Our weapons effective range is 236 meters.

00:47:22.088 --> 00:47:26.355
So we should look at the distance marker
and try to keep that in mind.

00:47:26.355 --> 00:47:28.988
Now, normally
our weapon would be effective

00:47:28.988 --> 00:47:32.505
at this range,
but against this enemy, it's not.

00:47:32.505 --> 00:47:35.588
That's because this enemy
has a very high defense.

00:47:35.588 --> 00:47:38.855
Therefore,
our weapon is ricocheting at range.

00:47:38.855 --> 00:47:43.388
Remember to keep an eye out for this
ricochet notification while you play.

00:47:43.388 --> 00:47:44.355
If it appears,

00:47:44.355 --> 00:47:49.038
it means you'll do little to no damage
unless you get within your ideal range,

00:47:49.038 --> 00:47:53.238
at which point, attack power is guaranteed
without ricochets.

00:47:53.238 --> 00:47:57.455
For this weapon,
our ideal range is 115 meters.

00:47:57.455 --> 00:48:01.121
Because my ace is slow
and my weaponry is good in short

00:48:01.121 --> 00:48:04.488
bursts, I'm going to use the environment
to my advantage here.

00:48:04.488 --> 00:48:06.071
By peeking around this corner.

00:48:06.071 --> 00:48:10.105
Whenever my missiles are up,
I can build up ACS strain at range

00:48:10.121 --> 00:48:11.555
with no risk.

00:48:11.555 --> 00:48:15.338
And when the enemy comes close to me,
that's great because my machine guns

00:48:15.338 --> 00:48:19.655
can take it to a breaking point
without it posing any threat.

00:48:19.655 --> 00:48:21.855
When playing,
consider your build strengths

00:48:21.855 --> 00:48:25.505
and consider the enemy's weaknesses
and come up with a plan.

00:48:25.505 --> 00:48:27.105
If that plan doesn't work.

00:48:27.105 --> 00:48:30.255
Reassess your build or reassess
your strategy.

00:48:30.255 --> 00:48:34.938
That's how you overcome
difficulty in Armored Core.

00:48:34.938 --> 00:48:35.988
See the bottom right?

00:48:35.988 --> 00:48:39.754
That's where you'll be able to note
that you've unlocked a checkpoint.

00:48:39.754 --> 00:48:42.004
We're done here and we can proceed.

00:48:42.004 --> 00:48:45.004
But while we're here,
we might as well take out the cannons

00:48:45.004 --> 00:48:47.104
that were pestering us on the wall.

00:48:47.104 --> 00:48:48.338
These are optional enemies.

00:48:48.338 --> 00:48:52.204
But every kill rewards us
with credits in the bottom right.

00:48:52.204 --> 00:48:56.504
Therefore, destroying these cannons is
well worth it if we have the time.

00:48:56.504 --> 00:48:58.604
Our objective
marker tells us where to go. Now.

00:48:58.604 --> 00:49:01.388
But there are often other ways
to your objective as well.

00:49:01.388 --> 00:49:04.688
For example, if we take this door
above our objective marker,

00:49:04.688 --> 00:49:08.888
we can actually sneak inside
and get an advantageous high position

00:49:08.888 --> 00:49:10.338
over our enemies.

00:49:10.338 --> 00:49:14.404
There's a marker here that denotes
that they're unaware of us right now.

00:49:14.404 --> 00:49:15.788
Damage dealt to these enemies

00:49:15.788 --> 00:49:20.271
during this time
will result in higher impact and ACS Strain

00:49:21.338 --> 00:49:23.854
The final boss of this mission
is a tough one.

00:49:23.854 --> 00:49:25.388
It's the juggernaut.

00:49:25.388 --> 00:49:29.138
The juggernaut has armor
that negates all damage from the front.

00:49:29.138 --> 00:49:32.104
Note the armor notification here.

00:49:32.104 --> 00:49:35.938
However, its sides back
and top are vulnerable.

00:49:36.004 --> 00:49:40.271
So a build that has great
generator capacity and high boosts.

00:49:40.271 --> 00:49:44.704
A thrust speed will be able to maneuver
in the air and get over the juggernaut

00:49:44.804 --> 00:49:46.304
more effectively.

00:49:46.304 --> 00:49:50.321
Any build can beat the juggernaut, but
if you're using a build that has to return

00:49:50.321 --> 00:49:54.188
to the ground more often,
then you might have a harder time.

00:49:54.188 --> 00:49:56.688
But if you fail during this mission,
don't worry.

00:49:56.688 --> 00:49:58.238
The game's checkpoints

00:49:58.238 --> 00:50:02.254
system will instantly allow you
to restart at difficult encounters.

00:50:02.254 --> 00:50:05.654
What's more, if you have the parts,
then you can consider quickly

00:50:05.654 --> 00:50:08.887
switching up your build here
by entering assembly.

00:50:08.887 --> 00:50:12.137
Remember how I said
my build has some extra load free?

00:50:12.137 --> 00:50:15.487
Well, I'm going to make use of that now
and I'm going to equip

00:50:15.487 --> 00:50:18.937
two heavy bazookas instead of my machine
guns.

00:50:18.937 --> 00:50:21.071
These bazookas deal explosive damage,

00:50:21.071 --> 00:50:25.054
which will help me to stagger
the juggernaut much more effectively.

00:50:25.054 --> 00:50:29.287
The juggernaut is a slow, large target,
so the usual drawbacks of

00:50:29.287 --> 00:50:32.537
using bazookas
don't really come into play here.

00:50:32.537 --> 00:50:36.254
Another thing to consider during
this fight is whether you want to use

00:50:36.287 --> 00:50:39.287
target assist with R3 or not.

00:50:39.287 --> 00:50:43.054
It's true
that yes, target assist is generally great

00:50:43.054 --> 00:50:47.854
if we're just facing one singular enemy,
but there are absolutely exceptions

00:50:47.854 --> 00:50:50.587
to this rule.
The juggernaut is one of them.

00:50:50.587 --> 00:50:53.087
Target
Assist has a few drawbacks in this fight.

00:50:53.087 --> 00:50:56.987
For one, it forces you to move at an angle
respective to the enemy.

00:50:56.987 --> 00:51:01.821
This is especially concerning if I try
to assault boost towards the juggernaut.

00:51:01.904 --> 00:51:06.304
Doing this while locked on means
I'm assault boosting right into its front.

00:51:06.304 --> 00:51:08.471
That's not where I want to go.

00:51:08.471 --> 00:51:12.854
With target lock disabled, we're able
to move more freely around the enemy.

00:51:12.854 --> 00:51:16.371
What's more, our assault boost is free
to be aimed above or

00:51:16.371 --> 00:51:21.787
beside the juggernaut, better enabling us
to get around it as an added incentive.

00:51:21.787 --> 00:51:22.937
Playing without target

00:51:22.937 --> 00:51:26.870
lock actually increases
the tracking strength of your lock on so

00:51:26.870 --> 00:51:31.337
our shots will find the target more often
if we don't use target assist.

00:51:31.337 --> 00:51:34.637
Consider all of these things
and your overall skill level

00:51:34.637 --> 00:51:39.487
when considering whether to use
target lock in your missions.

00:51:39.487 --> 00:51:41.720
Shortly after Operation Wall Climber,

00:51:41.720 --> 00:51:44.104
two new menus will become available: 

00:51:44.104 --> 00:51:46.937
the arena and OS tuning

00:51:46.937 --> 00:51:51.220
The arena is a ranked simulator
where you can fight enemy AC.

00:51:51.220 --> 00:51:55.687
There's no healing or multiple enemies,
just a fair one on one fight.

00:51:55.687 --> 00:51:57.437
Here you can climb in the ranks.

00:51:57.437 --> 00:52:00.620
And while we can only 
fight against F-rank opponents

00:52:00.620 --> 00:52:04.270
at this early stage of the game,
more enemies will be unlocked.

00:52:04.270 --> 00:52:06.287
As you progress in your missions.

00:52:06.287 --> 00:52:08.137
And the arena is absolutely something

00:52:08.137 --> 00:52:12.170
you should be clearing
as soon as new AC fights become available.

00:52:12.170 --> 00:52:17.020
Not only is this invaluable practice for
some of the hardest fights in the game,

00:52:17.020 --> 00:52:21.670
not only are you rewarded with credits
with no repair or ammunition costs,

00:52:21.670 --> 00:52:26.737
the most important thing is that you're
also rewarded with a crucial resource.

00:52:26.737 --> 00:52:28.370
OST Chips.

00:52:28.370 --> 00:52:29.870
OST Chips are a resource

00:52:29.870 --> 00:52:33.937
that can be spent on various
categorical upgrades for your AC.

00:52:33.937 --> 00:52:37.570
This is done in the OS tuning menu,
and once you're here

00:52:37.570 --> 00:52:39.787
you'll be met with a series of upgrades.

00:52:39.787 --> 00:52:43.987
Some of the upgrades in these menus
are intended for more experienced players.

00:52:43.987 --> 00:52:48.503
For example, few players will ever find
they need to aim manually

00:52:48.503 --> 00:52:51.287
or to enter a mission while overburdened.

00:52:51.287 --> 00:52:55.787
So be careful not to waste your points
on upgrades that you won't use.

00:52:55.787 --> 00:53:01.537
That said, you can recover your spent
OST chips by pressing triangle or Y.

00:53:01.537 --> 00:53:06.487
This will cost you 4000 credits
for every OS upgrade you need to undo,

00:53:07.037 --> 00:53:08.203
but some upgrades here

00:53:08.203 --> 00:53:12.070
will make any player stronger
regardless of their skill level.

00:53:12.070 --> 00:53:15.137
While I'd recommend you read through
and consider these yourself,

00:53:15.137 --> 00:53:19.420
let's go through each category now
and pick out a few priorities

00:53:19.420 --> 00:53:21.137
in terms of system unlocks.

00:53:21.137 --> 00:53:24.703
One that I'd absolutely recommend
everyone unlock eventually

00:53:24.703 --> 00:53:26.353
is the kick function.

00:53:26.353 --> 00:53:29.570
With this enabled,
you'll be able to do a melee slam

00:53:29.570 --> 00:53:33.887
at the end of your assault boost
by pressing L3 once again.

00:53:33.970 --> 00:53:35.437
This is especially great.

00:53:35.437 --> 00:53:38.503
While you're hard
locked onto an enemy with target assist

00:53:38.503 --> 00:53:43.520
and it's the perfect capstone to an enemy
who is almost guard broken

00:53:43.520 --> 00:53:47.270
because it saves
you having to expend ammunition

00:53:47.270 --> 00:53:50.320
on breaking their guard
and it leaves your ammunition

00:53:50.320 --> 00:53:54.437
free to capitalize on their broken
guard instead.

00:53:54.437 --> 00:53:56.503
Next, let's talk expansions.

00:53:56.503 --> 00:54:01.187
Once unlocked, expansions
can be slotted into your AC’s assembly.

00:54:01.187 --> 00:54:04.670
And while you can only equip one expansion
at a time,

00:54:04.670 --> 00:54:09.403
you can invest into unlocking
multiple charges of each expansion.

00:54:09.403 --> 00:54:13.670
However, note that unlocking
multiple expansion charges is expensive

00:54:13.670 --> 00:54:18.520
and there's a cooldown period
after using an expansion charge.

00:54:18.520 --> 00:54:21.253
By default,
expansions are activated by pressing

00:54:21.253 --> 00:54:25.270
L3 and triangle,
or Y, simaltenuously.

00:54:25.270 --> 00:54:29.053
However, you can switch these controls
in the game settings here.

00:54:29.053 --> 00:54:32.920
Personally,
I prefer type B, which allows activation

00:54:32.920 --> 00:54:37.053
with L3 and R3, which is easy to remember.

00:54:37.053 --> 00:54:41.236
When your just starting out, It is easy
to forget to use your expansions.

00:54:41.236 --> 00:54:44.420
So if you're new to the game,
then I'd actually recommend

00:54:44.420 --> 00:54:47.686
that you choose a passive expansion
instead.

00:54:47.686 --> 00:54:50.270
For example, this is terminal armor.

00:54:50.270 --> 00:54:54.220
Once equipped, it's always active
and will always keep you alive at

00:54:54.220 --> 00:54:59.686
1 AP for a few more seconds in a situation
where you would have been destroyed,

00:54:59.686 --> 00:55:05.386
this can give you valuable time to heal
or just survive a little longer.

00:55:05.386 --> 00:55:08.770
I really can't overstate
how useful passive upgrades

00:55:08.770 --> 00:55:12.620
are in an input heavy game
like Armored Core six.

00:55:12.620 --> 00:55:16.120
After terminal armor, I'd recommend
getting the early ranks of many

00:55:16.120 --> 00:55:17.470
passive upgrades.

00:55:17.470 --> 00:55:21.886
You can't go too wrong here,
and by investing in passive upgrades,

00:55:21.886 --> 00:55:26.453
you can rest
that your AC is becoming more powerful.

00:55:27.136 --> 00:55:28.720
And that concludes the guide.

00:55:28.720 --> 00:55:30.370
Thank you for watching.

00:55:30.370 --> 00:55:34.336
More Tips
Lore and Secrets about Armored Core six.

00:55:34.336 --> 00:55:36.286
Consider subscribing to my channel.

00:55:38.088 --> 00:55:39.571
Good luck everybody.

00:55:39.971 --> 00:55:41.254
Get to work.

